==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|сѣсть||ru-PRO}}

===Etymology===
{{root|ru|ine-pro|*sed-}}
From {{inh|ru|orv|сѣсти}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*sěsti}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-bsl-pro|*sḗˀstei}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-pro|*sed-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-сесть.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|сесть|pf|impf=сади́ться}}

# to [[sit]] down
#: {{uxi|ru|[[я|Я]] '''сел''' [[на]] [[диван|дива́н]] [[ря́дом]] [[с]] [[мой|мои́м]] [[друг|дру́гом]].|I '''sat''' on the couch next to my friend.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[я|Я]] '''се́ла''' [[бли́же]] [[к]] [[настольный|насто́льной]] [[лампа|ла́мпе]].|I '''sat''' near the tabletop lamp.}}
#* {{quote-book|ru|year=2011|author=w:ru:Виктор Пелевин<t:{{w|Victor Pelevin}}>|title=w:ru:S.N.U.F.F.|chapter=Ч. 1. Damsel in distress, 2|location=|publisher=|newversion=English translation from|translator2=w:Andrew Bromfield|title2=w:S.N.U.F.F.|location2=|publisher2=|year2=2014|page2=|pageurl2=|text=Пото́м ему́ стра́шно захоте́лось '''сесть''' на доро́гу, и не́ было никако́й возмо́жности противостоя́ть э́тому жела́нию. А когда́ он '''сел''', ста́ло я́сно, что на́до лечь, и он лёг.|t=Then he suddenly felt an overwhelming urge '''to sit down''' in the road, and the desire was absolutely impossible to resist. And once he '''sat down''', he realised he had to lie down, so he did.}}
# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} to be [[imprison]]ed
# to [[become]] [[flat]], to [[die]] {{q|of an electrical battery or accumulator}}
# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} to [[shrink]] {{q|of an item of clothing after laundry}}

